ecosystem_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  change: The local PHP preview no longer delegates arbitrary repository files to the built-in file server. Only manifest-declared static HTTPS readback paths are served, through direct files with canonical paths; normal page rendering is retained.
  boundary: Exact loopback Host plus GET or HEAD; private files, path aliases, linked files and directories, and other methods are rejected without reflecting paths or file content.
  verification: Eight executable checks passed, including every declared static GET and HEAD byte, live PHP negative requests, retired-route behavior, and a real directory-link probe. No fixtures remain in artifacts.
  coverage_gap: PHP has no Xdebug or PCOV coverage extension; real PHP and HTTP behavior checks are the closest automated evidence, not a percentage claim.
  publication: index.php changed. Existing package and deployment byte bindings require regeneration after the next content checkpoint; no publication or deployed-current claim is made.
  validator_change: Deployment transaction and hostile-gate tests now synthesize bounded filesystem/Git responses in memory instead of creating Git repositories, copied tools or public stages. A separate test reads the real canonical committed closure.
  validator_corrections: The CLI root declaration is repaired; the gate pin matches the committed TinyRustLM source-authority verifier; Git reads require the canonical repository and have a timeout; batch payloads are rehashed against their Git blob IDs instead of trusting matching headers.
  validator_verification: Twenty checks passed with zero skips, including the actual canonical CLI source gate, read-only Git closure and actual PowerShell rejection before deployment input. Whole-file Node coverage is 98.86 percent for the virtual fixture, 94.70 percent for the preflight and 74.17 percent for the deployment validator; the new root and payload checks executed.
  validator_evidence: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/deployment-validator-review.json
  validator_lessons: Current pins must follow reviewed committed consumers; page-preview success does not prove release entrypoints work; matching transport headers do not prove payload identity. No source copy or executable fixture is needed for these boundary cases.
  pending: Historical 1.8.3 stage removal is policy-blocked. Current package-only C2 is 07a2502, but the deployment generator correctly rejected the surviving stage and left old metadata unchanged. Remaining copied-source transaction/archive tests still require review. No publication or deployed-current result is claimed.

canonical_release_tools_cleanup_2026_09_12:
  implementation: Package and deployment generators emit metadata to stdout only. The PowerShell entrypoint validates canonical public bytes through the shared validator; 959 removed legacy lines include unreachable transport, credential and receipt code. The unused staged-file validator was removed.
  correctness: Exact canonical root and manifest; regular public files and complete Git/worktree paths including ignored extras; C2 ancestry and byte identities; retired stage absence; explicit LF attributes; Node startup environment disabled across both subprocess calls.
  owner_policy: MiniModel.org is the default discovery/P2P source and may operate initial server seeds. Hugging Face, local import, conversion and manual peer/IP settings belong under Advanced. These requirements are not live availability evidence.
  verification: 56 checks ran; 55 passed, one correctly fails because the reviewed 1.8.3 stage remains. Zero skipped or cancelled. Actual PHP GET/HEAD and negative route checks passed. Actual PowerShell with hostile Node options reached and rejected the retired stage. Owned scratch was removed.
  coverage: Validator 90.97 percent lines; public policy 96.80; virtual fixture 96.81; scratch helper 100. Branch coverage and limits are in the compact proof.
  evidence: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/canonical-release-tools-review.json
  retirement: All 27 stage files match immutable Git commit 24e4f875a0e508827e6ddf6f94664e927261fbd5 and the compact review; zero unique files. Deletion was rejected with blocked by policy. The exact owner-run script and combined ecosystem command passed WhatIf only. No storage recovery is claimed.

